  "title": "Iqa‘ Baladi 4/4",
  "subtitle": "(also called Masmudi Saghir)",
  "description": "Iqa‘ Baladi (Masmudi Saghir)",
  "lang": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    "Iqa‘ Baladi is a very common iqa‘ in the Near Eastern Arabic vocal repertoire. It is also called Masmudi Saghir, \"saghir\" meaning little in Arabic, to distinguish it from Masmudi Kabir, which spans two 4/4 measures instead of one. Baladi modulates frequently to Maqsum and back, as well as to Malfuf (using 2 measures of Malfuf to 1 measure of Baladi)."
  ],
  "text": "Iqa‘ Baladi 4/4 (also called Masmudi Saghir ) Iqa‘ Index Pronunciation of Baladi Iqa‘ Baladi is a very common iqa‘ in the Near Eastern Arabic vocal repertoire. It is also called Masmudi Saghir , \"saghir\" meaning little in Arabic, to distinguish it from Masmudi Kabir , which spans two 4/4 measures instead of one. Baladi modulates frequently to Maqsum and back, as well as to Malfuf (using 2 measures of Malfuf to 1 measure of Baladi). ‘Aziza (1955) Instrumental Composition Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (from the movie ‘Aziza, 1955) Talumuni Wa Lam Tarthu Li Hali Hassan al-Haffar Qadd Malik Ya Hilwa Muhammad Khayri Iqa‘ Baladi 4/4 Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan",
